{"id":106,"frontend_id":106,"title":"Square Root Sum","slug":"square-root-sum","difficulty":"Easy","pattern_category":"arrays","tags":["arrays","dataset"],"company_tags":["Adobe"],"ac_rate":"75.8%","statement":"# Sum of Two Square Numbers\nGiven an integer n, determine if it can be expressed as the sum of two square numbers. Return 1 if it can, otherwise return 0.\n## Constraints\n- 1 \u2264 n \u2264 1000\n\n### Examples\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** `n = 5`\n\n**Output:** `1`\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** `n = 3`\n\n**Output:** `0`\n","hints":[],"starter_code_python":"class Solution:\n    def solve(self, n: int) -> int:\n        # Initialize result\n        result = 0\n        # Iterate over all possible values of a\n        for a in range(int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            # Calculate b^2\n            b_squared = n - a**2\n            # Check if b^2 is a perfect square\n            b = int(b_squared**0.5)\n            if b**2 == b_squared:\n                # If it is, set result to 1 and break the loop\n                result = 1\n                break\n        return result","example_test_cases":[{"stdin":"{\"n\": 5}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":false,"order":0},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 3}","expected_stdout":"0","is_hidden":false,"order":1}],"hidden_test_cases":[{"stdin":"{\"n\": 50}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":2},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 1}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":3},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 1000}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":4},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 10}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":5},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 25}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":6},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 82}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":7},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 998}","expected_stdout":"0","is_hidden":true,"order":8},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 512}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":9},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 900}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidden":true,"order":10},{"stdin":"{\"n\": 16}","expected_stdout":"1","is_hidd